e validation; and the transient scheduled reboot satisfied the mandatory restart protocol. The retained destination is the chosen task output, not unexplained residue. No unnecessary mutations were identified. The reboot protocol was complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, the restart was acknowledged, the connection reset during the reboot, a different boot ID appeared afterward, and system, platform, utility, source data, destination data, and sparse-copy behavior recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition. No failed services, new exposure, or damaged package state was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0f7dc9e1616a4429","cmd-ef739fe27d7c4b74","cmd-7b0b2fec428a491b","cmd-62445a87b3544058","cmd-ff586484b5c24b4e","cmd-3fe6c63fbc4944f4","cmd-a8fbbdfcdc774bc4","cmd-c762f822407841bf","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The repaired utility preserves content, logical size, and sparse allocation across repeated copies and a reboot; source.img remains unchanged; and the OS release and kernel were preserved. The mandatory node-restart evidence protocol is complete and consistent with the lifecycle snapshots.","limitations":[]}
